component SigilSemanticCompiler {
  goal {
    Turn authored Sigil sources into resolved SourceTrees, compute design
    results from caller supplied language interpretation, and compare design
    commitments with supplied implementation readings.
  }

  interface {
    *language interpretation* Caller supplied semantic readings consumed by
    computed design claims; the compiler does not invoke a model.

    *CompilerCommands* Provide one native executable for tree inspection,
    computed design claims, implementation alignment, and disposable cache
    cleanup. The executable launches no model or interpreter; callers prepare
    and supply external readings.

    *SourceTrees* Parse each source into a content-addressed tree and resolve
    names against imported component interfaces. Expose trees and optional
    Facet differences through the tree command.
  }
}
